  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Campus Life",
      "value": "<p>Student life on campus is full of activity. Welcome week is the student orientation event that welcomes students from all different walks of life to find their tribe amongst the 150 student clubs organized on campus. More cultural festivals, musical performances and academic speaker events occur on campus throughout the year, so students are always aware of nearby activities to enjoy. Similarly, volunteering opportunities are frequently communicated to students so they can make a difference in the community and boost their CVs simultaneously. The fitness centers on campus run classes for students to have fun and keep fit, with a sports hall and swimming pool also easy to access throughout the year. A community feel runs throughout the campus so students can create a comfortable home away from home.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>WSU empowers their students with six libraries across its campuses that are stocked with all the learning materials a student could need in digital and print form. The University is dedicated to continual development and innovation, making its facilities modern and accessible to the student body. Various first-rate laboratories and research centers are in place at the university, and performance spaces such as theaters and music rooms for students to have an artistic outlet.</p><p>The student center is given suitable materials for student organizations and support teams to thrive as this leading university prioritizes the student experience.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Sydney offers its residents a high quality of living, and Western Sydney University provides its students a range of on-campus accommodation. Among their six campus villages, students can choose between studio apartments or single or shared rooms, with catering available, so they benefit from enjoying cooked meals in addition to the range of food options available on campus. Student support services are also available 24/7, and there is convenient access to the campus library.</p><p>Homestay arrangements are a fantastic option for international students who want the comfort of living with a trusted local family who can help them better acclimate to the English language and embrace the culture. Students wishing to live independently in a private rental off-campus can contact the university’s accommodation support officer for help and advice.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "City Life",
      "value": "<p>Sydney is famed for being multicultural and inclusive of all cultures, often in the top five on ranking lists of the best places to live in the world. The sandy shores in Sydney are lined with cafes and bars for students to enjoy some much-needed downtime, and numerous festivals take place throughout the year, with some free events included too. The different campuses at WSU are conveniently located close to nearby towns with award-winning restaurants and regular events, so students can always find life-enhancing activities.</p>",
      "image": "",
      "highlightType": "Infos"
    }
  ],
